  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Jebel Musa</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The northern peaks of Jebel Musa, a mountain on the African side of the Strait of Gibraltar, are usually identified as the southern Pillar of Hercules. They share toponymy with and lie to the west of the ancient settlement of Septem (modern Ceuta).",
